# Fableland — Hit Feedback GDD

How a hit, a jump, a death — any moment worth noticing — is told to the player: the **cue
bus** gameplay raises, **hit-stop**, and the **feel** layer (camera shake, kick, roll, zoom
punch, hit flash). It is the foundation the VFX and audio layers plug into: they listen to
the same bus and never touch gameplay.

Implementation: `Scripts/Gameplay/Combat/{Cue,BodyFeedback,HitInfo}.cs`,
`Scripts/Data/FeedbackTable.cs`, `Scripts/Foundation/FeedbackSettings.cs`,
`Scripts/Presentation/Feel/{FeelDirector,FeelTable}.cs`, `Scripts/UI/ShakeCamera2D.cs`.
First landed in **v0.11.2**. Research behind the numbers:
`Docs/Research/R2-vfx-feel-research.md` (cited below as **R2**; its §6 lists which sources
were read and which are from memory).

> **Nobody has watched this yet.** Every number here was reasoned from the research and from
> pixels at 32 px/m, and verified by a headless check (§10) — which proves the mechanisms,
> not the look. The first job of whoever plays it is the verify-by-eye pass
> (`50-ART-AUDIO.md` §6); expect to retune §3 and §5.

---

## 1. Principles

1. **Gameplay raises, presentation listens.** A kit, a foe, a hazard or a mission says *what
   happened* and with what numbers; it never names a particle, a sound or a shake, and never
   calls a director. Adding an effect to a moment that already raises a cue touches no
   gameplay file.
2. **Hit-stop is per body, never `Engine.TimeScale`.** A global freeze also freezes timers,
   input and the UI, and Godot's own docs warn against a zero time scale [R2 A1.13, verified
   against the Godot `Engine` class reference]. Only the two bodies of a hit hold; a
   projectile's owner never does [R2 A1.2, verified: SmashWiki, *Hitlag*].
3. **Hit-stop is the only feel element that changes the simulation**, so it is gameplay: it
   lives in the bodies and its numbers in `Scripts/Data/FeedbackTable.cs`. Everything else
   observes, and may be dropped (a setting, a budget) without changing a fight.
4. **Dynamic range is the point.** A graze gets a number and a tint; an ultimate gets
   everything. Small hits are carried by the kick and the flash, not by shake — shake is
   seasoning ("Camera shake is like salt" — Squirrel Eiserloh, GDC 2016) [R2 A2.4, verified].
5. **Shake is trauma², smooth, capped per tier** [R2 A2.1, A2.3, verified: Eiserloh's
   slides]: smooth noise instead of a new random offset each frame, and a ceiling per tier
   so a crowd of small hits can never shake like a big one.
6. **Flash means "hit"; blink means "cannot be hit".** Foes no longer blink when struck —
   they have no i-frames [R2 A3.4, convention, from memory].
7. **Safe by default.** The photosensitivity limits in §5.4 hold whatever the settings are
   [R2 A3.1–A3.3, verified: WCAG 2.3.1 and Xbox Accessibility Guideline 118 — the stricter
   area figure of the two is used]. Settings are the second line, not the first.
8. **Effects and hitboxes come from one number.** A cue carries the attack's real reach,
   box and direction (`50-ART-AUDIO.md` §1).
9. **No per-event garbage** (`T40` §2): cues are structs keyed by constant strings; raising
   14 000 of them with the feel director acting on each allocates 0 bytes (measured, §10).

---

## 2. The cue bus

```
GAMEPLAY      a moment happens ──▶ CueBus.Emit / Start / Stop / EmitHit      (static, no listener known)
PRESENTATION  FeelDirector  ◀── CueBus.Raised, CueBus.HitLanded              (this document)
              (next) VfxDirector, AudioDirector ◀── the same four events
```

| Type | What it is |
|---|---|
| `Cue` | A moment: `Owner`, `OwnerClass`, `Action`, `Variant`, `Tag`, `Source`, `Position`, `Direction`, `Size` (reach / radius, px), `Extents` (a box's half-extents, px), `Magnitude`, `Side`. |
| `HitCue` | A hit that landed — both ends of it: victim (`Victim`, `VictimOwner`, `VictimClass`, `VictimIsPlayer`), attack (`Attacker`, `AttackOwner`, `AttackClass`, `AttackAction`, `AttackVariant`, `Ranged`), and the result (`Weight`, `Damage`, `Knockback`, `Position`, `Direction`, `Killed`, `VictimStop`). |
| `CueBus` | `Emit(body, action, …)` / `EmitAt(owner, action, position, …)` for one-shots; `Start` / `Stop` (and `StartAt` / `StopAt`) for anything that lasts; `EmitHit` (the two hit intakes only). Events: `Raised`, `HitLanded`, `LoopStarted`, `LoopStopped`. |
| `IFeedbackBody` | What presentation may know of a body: `FeedbackId`, `FeedbackClass`, `Side`, `FeedbackState`, `FeedbackCenter`, `FeedbackRadius`, `InHitStop`, `FlashTint(colour, seconds)`. Read-only or purely visual. |
| `CueTable<T>` | A director's table, keyed (owner, action), resolved **owner → class → `any`**. |

**The key is two strings**, so nothing is concatenated per event. `Owner` is whose look and
sound it is — a content id in snake_case (`pomegraknight`, `crab`) or a system (`world`,
`hazard`, `flow`). `Action` is what happened, dotted and lower-case (`ba.swing`, `land`).
A director looks up (owner, action); with no row, (the owner's class, action); with no row,
(`any`, action). So a new character looks and sounds like *a fighter* before it has a row of
its own, and one `any/land` row serves every body in the game.

Content ids and classes:

| Body | `FeedbackId` | Class |
|---|---|---|
| Pomegraknight · Cleopastar · Pixolotl · PumpKing · Sifu Pangda | `pomegraknight` · `cleopastar` · `pixolotl` · `pumpking` · `sifu_pangda` | `fighter` |
| BOSS PumpKing (the same kit on the Foe side) | `pumpking` | `boss` |
| Crab · Seagull · the stand-in boss | `crab` · `seagull` · `boss_crab` | `foe` |
| Destroy objective · the Protect core | `destroy_objective` · `protect_core` | `objective` |
| A projectile with no body at hand (a seed whose owner left, PumpKing's head) | its owner's id | `projectile` |

A class overrides `FeedbackId` with a constant; the default is its class name in snake_case.

**Rules for whoever raises a cue**

- Raise it on the line where the moment happens, with that moment's real geometry.
- Never read anything back; nothing a listener does may change a fight.
- One-shots are `Emit`; anything that lasts is `Start` … `Stop`, same source, owner and
  action. A body stops its own loops when it dies and when it leaves the tree.
- Pass constant strings. A fan of projectiles is one cue with a count, not a cue per seed.

**Rules for whoever listens**

- Subscribe in `_EnterTree`, unsubscribe in `_ExitTree` (`T10` §1) — the bus is static.
- A `Source` may be freed by the time you act later: `GodotObject.IsInstanceValid` before
  calling into it; match loops with `ReferenceEquals`.
- Draw your own randomness; never a run's `DetRandom` stream.
- A listener that throws is logged and skipped. That is a safety net, not a licence.

---

## 3. How heavy a hit is

A hit is measured by its **impact score D**: the damage it dealt after mitigation — or, on
the body the player wears, `150 × damage / MaxHP`, so a hit is felt by what it costs. D
picks the tier; an attack may instead **name** its weight (`HitInfo.Weight`), which holds
it in that tier whatever buffs do to its damage.

| Tier | `HitWeight` | D | Victim stop | Attacker stop (melee) | Shake add / cap | Kick | Roll | Flash | Zoom punch |
|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|
| T0 | `Graze` | < 8 | — | — | — | — | — | tint, 33 ms | — |
| T1 | `Light` | 8–24 | 33–58 ms | 23–41 ms | +0.15 / 0.30 (2.7 px) | 2 px | — | 33 ms | — |
| T2 | `Medium` | 25–59 | 60–114 ms | 42–80 ms | +0.25 / 0.50 (7.5 px) | 4 px | — | 50 ms | — |
| T3 | `Heavy` | 60–149 | 116–180 ms | 81–126 ms | +0.40 / 0.75 (17 px) | 7 px | small | 67 ms | 1.02× |
| T4 | `Massive` | ≥ 150 | 180 ms | 126 ms | +0.55 / 0.90 (24 px) | 10 px | under 1° | 83 ms | 1.04× |
| | the hit that **kills** | | the victim is not held | +33 ms, at least 67 ms | +0.10 on both | | | | at least 1.015× |

- **Victim stop** = `clamp(20 ms + 1.6 ms · D, 33 ms, 180 ms)`; a graze holds nobody.
  Smash-shaped (a constant plus a slope in damage, capped), with smaller numbers: a roguelike
  repeats a jab thousands of times [R2 A1.1, verified: SmashWiki's hitlag formulas].
- **Attacker stop** = 0.7 × that — shorter, so landing a blow never feels like losing
  control. (In Smash both ends stop equally [R2 A1.2]; the shorter attacker stop is our
  choice.)
- **The player being hit** is held at least 50 ms and at most 150 ms, and the camera reads
  one tier up: being hit must be felt more than hitting.
- Worked examples (`FeedbackTable.SelfTest`): a 15-damage slash is Light — victim 44 ms
  (3 ticks), attacker 31 ms (2); Pomegraknight's third slash (30) is Medium — 68 ms; a crab's
  18 on a 200-HP fighter scores 13.5 — Light, held 50 ms.

Shake pixels are `trauma² × 30`. They are small on purpose (principle 4) and smaller than
the flat 0.35 every hit used to add; retune by eye.

---

## 4. Hit-stop rules

1. **What holds.** A body in hit-stop holds its **motion and its animation**. **Every clock
   keeps running** — cooldowns, ammo, statuses, the gain-no (stun) window — and **abilities
   are still read**, so no DPS, cooldown or timing in a fight depends on how often anyone
   was stopped, and a press during a stop is never lost. Jump, the one edge read in the
   physics loop, is remembered across a stop and fires on the tick after it.
2. **Who is held.** The **victim** — by the hit intake (`TakeHit`), from the resolved
   weight. The **attacker** of a blow of its own body — **once per swing**, for the heaviest
   hit the swing landed, never per victim (`CharacterController.MeleeCone` / `SwingStop`;
   `BaseFoe.Strike`). **Projectiles, fields and ticks (`HitInfo.Ranged`) never hold their
   owner.** Hazard ticks and damage over time hold nobody: they are not hits.
3. **A body that dies is not held.** A foe frees itself the frame it dies; a fighter has its
   own exit. (Holding the killing frame — R2's "holds its flash, then bursts" — needs a death
   delay; §9.)
4. **Stops take the max, never add.** A request while held can only lengthen the hold.
5. **Re-arm.** A body that left a stop is not stopped again for 0.10 s.
6. **Budget.** Every granted second comes out of a 0.18 s budget that refills at 0.15 s per
   second, so under any sustained stream of hits a body is held about 15 % of the time and
   no more (without it, a 52 ms stop every 0.15 s would hold a foe a third of the time).
   One isolated stop of any length always fits; a three-slash combo fits.
7. **Counted in world time**, in the physics loop (`HitStopClock`): never the held body's own
   time (it would never wake), never `GetActDelta` / `LocalTimeRate` — Pixolotl overrides
   that rate and her bubbles and the item runtime read it, so they would freeze with her.
8. **A held body reports `Velocity` zero** and keeps its two velocity channels; it resumes
   with the motion it had, plus the knockback the hit added (the shove starts when the stop
   lets go).
9. **The setting.** `FeedbackSettings.HitStop` scales every stop; 0 switches it off.
10. **Kits that move themselves**
    | Kit | Decision | How |
    |---|---|---|
    | Sifu Pangda — palm lunge, Heli dive, Heli dash | **Holds** with the body (a stopped palm keeps its full lunge) | `if (HitStopHeld) return;` after `base._PhysicsProcess` |
    | PumpKing — Soul Form | **Holds**; the soul counts its own stop, because it never reaches the base tick | `if (HoldForHitStop(delta)) return;` |
    | PumpKing's head | **Exempt** — a projectile: never held, its hits are ranged, its owner is never held | — |
    | Cleopastar's star | **Exempt** — a projectile and a platform; her hits from it should be marked ranged when her kit is wired | — |
    | Pixolotl — rewind | **Untouched** — it runs on her own clock in the process loop | — |

    A kit that moves the body without going through the base tick calls
    `HoldForHitStop`; one that moves it after the base tick reads `HitStopHeld`; never both.

---

## 5. Feel: what the director does with a hit

`FeelDirector` (a presentation autoload) listens to the bus and reads `FeelTable`.

### 5.1 Camera

- **Shake.** Per-tier trauma with a cap (table in §3). **Every hit that lands in one frame
  is one camera event**: the heaviest adds its tier's trauma, each further victim a sliver
  (+0.03, at most five), all under the heaviest tier's cap — a swing through a crowd cannot
  sum past it, and neither can a stream of hits frame after frame. The offset is read from
  smooth noise (it reverses about twenty times a second — measured), so it looks the same at
  any frame rate.
- **Kick.** A shove along the blow that springs back in about a tenth of a second; on the
  player it points away from whatever hit them.
- **Roll.** Under a degree, for Heavy and Massive only. The camera ignores rotation except
  while a roll is playing.
- **Zoom punch.** In over 30 ms, held 80 ms, back in 160 ms. Capped at 4 % for a hit,
  because damage numbers are world-space text and blur under zoom [R2 B9.16, verified].
- **The tsunami's sustained channel** (`SetSustainedTrauma`) is unchanged and shares the
  setting.

### 5.2 Named moments

| Cue | Beat |
|---|---|
| `flow` / `boss.defeated` | Trauma 1.0, full roll, zoom 1.10× (in 0.10 s, held 0.30 s, back in 0.60 s), one 100 ms flash **on the boss** — never the screen |
| `flow` / `player.down` | Trauma +0.60 (cap 0.90), zoom 1.06× |
| `pumpking` / `ba.explode` | Trauma +0.40 (cap 0.75) — the blast shakes even when it catches nobody (not a dud) |
| `any` / `hurt.tick`, on the player only | A tint, at most one per 0.34 s however many kinds of damage are ticking; a Light shake at most once a second |

### 5.3 The flash

A body flashes through **one channel of its own**: for a few frames its sprites are drawn
through a tiny shader that pulls them toward one colour and keeps their alpha — a
silhouette, which `Modulate` (a multiply) cannot do. The material is lent to the sprites
only while the flash runs. It never writes `Modulate`, `SelfModulate` or `Visible`: those
stay with the status tints, the telegraph tint, the i-frame blink and the defeat fade.

- **Light or dark, by the arena.** `flow`/`arena.enter` carries how light the backdrop is.
  At 0.80 or more (Banboo Maze's bare paper, Ghost Town's cream — about 0.9) a body flashes
  **ink** (`#14171A`); otherwise **white**. A sky-blue canvas (0.76) and an unknown one keep
  white.
- **A graze only tints** (35 %). With `FeedbackSettings.Flash` at 0 every flash is that tint:
  the hit must stay readable.

### 5.4 Photosensitivity limits (hold whatever the settings)

- Flashes that start within 0.1 s of each other are one flashing **moment**. At most **six**
  bodies flash at full strength in a moment; the rest tint.
- A moment whose flashing bodies cover more than **2.5 % of the view** is a **large flash**;
  no more than **three** may start in any second. The fourth is tinted.
- No flash colour is a saturated red (`R / (R+G+B) < 0.8`), no flash is longer than 100 ms,
  and there is **no full-screen flash anywhere**.
- Hazard and DoT pulses are merged to one per kind every 0.35 s, and the player's tint for
  them fires at most once per 0.34 s across all kinds (under 3 Hz).
- Not done: a Harding-style test of real footage (XAG 118 asks for one). The 35 % tint is
  itself a luminance change; on a large body it could still count as a flash.

---

## 6. The cue vocabulary

The work order for VFX and audio. *Italic* = where it is raised.

### 6.1 Hits — `CueBus.HitLanded`

One `HitCue` per hit that landed, from `CharacterController.TakeHit` and `BaseFoe.TakeHit`.
The attack names in use today:

| `AttackOwner` / `AttackAction` | Variant | Kind | Raised by |
|---|---|---|---|
| `pomegraknight` / `ba` | combo stage 1–3 | melee | *Pomegraknight.HandleBA → MeleeCone* |
| `pomegraknight` / `s1.tornado` | tick 1–5 | ranged, named Light | *Pomegraknight.TornadoHit* |
| `pomegraknight` / `s2.seed` | — | ranged | *PomeSeed.OnBodyEntered* |
| `pumpking` / `ba.head` · `ba.explode` | — | ranged | *PumpKingHead.TryStrike · DealExplosion* |
| `pumpking` / `ult.pumpkin` · `ult.blast` | — | ranged (no shove; never holds him) | *PrisonPumpkin.TryStrike · PumpKing.LandInPrisonMouth* — the Black Prison, §6.6 |
| *foe id* / `contact` | — | melee | *BaseFoe.TryContactDamage* |
| `seagull` / `s2.dash` · `s1.poop` | — | melee · ranged | *SeagullFoe.UpdateSkills · PoopProjectile.OnBodyEntered* |
| `hazard` / `tsunami` | — | ranged | *TsunamiHazard.OnBodyEntered* |
| `any` / `""` | — | — | every hit of a kit that is not wired yet (Cleopastar, Pixolotl, PumpKing's own, Sifu Pangda) |

### 6.2 Bodies — owner = the body's content id

| Action | Variant | Tag | Size · Magnitude · Direction · Position | Raised by |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| `spawn` | foe: its level | foe: `born` if it came out of a death | at the body, on its first tick | *CharacterController._PhysicsProcess · BaseFoe._PhysicsProcess* |
| `jump` | which jump of this airtime (1, 2…) | — ground · `air` · `swim` (a stroke in a soft volume) | magnitude = launch speed px/s · up · at the feet | *CharacterController._PhysicsProcess · BaseFoe.Integrate* |
| `land` | — | — | magnitude = impact speed px/s (192 and up) · down · at the feet | *same* |
| `death` | foe: its level | — | at the body | *CharacterController.Die · BaseFoe.Die · ProtectCore._Process* |
| `respawn` | — | — | at the respawn point | *CharacterController.Respawn* |
| `heal` | — | — | magnitude = amount | *CharacterController.Heal* |
| `hurt.tick` | — | `hazard` · `burn` · `on_fire` · `frozen` | magnitude = damage since the last one (at most one per kind per 0.35 s) | *HurtTickMeter ← ApplyHazard, DoT* |
| `ult.ready` | — | — | — | *CharacterController.GainUltCharge* |
| `switch.out` · `switch.in` | — | — | at the body; the incoming body raises no `spawn` | *GameManager.ReplacePlayerNode → NotifySwitchedOut / In* |
| `aggro` (foes) | — | — | direction = facing | *BaseFoe.EnterAggro* |
| `evolve` (foes) | the new level | — | — | *BaseFoe.Evolve* |
| `hurt` (`protect_core`) | — | — | magnitude = damage · direction = from the foe | *ProtectCore._Process* |
| **loop** `status.burning` · `status.on_fire` · `status.frozen` · `status.trapped` · `status.stunned` | — | — | — | *StatusLoops ← CharacterController._Process · BaseFoe._PhysicsProcess; stopped on death and on leaving the tree* |
| **loop** `telegraph` (foes) | — | — | size = the attack's reach · magnitude = the tell's seconds · direction | *BaseFoe.SetTelegraphTint / ClearTelegraphTint* |

### 6.3 Pomegraknight — the reference kit

| Action | Variant | Tag | Size · Magnitude · Direction · Position | Raised by |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| `ba.swing` | stage 1–3 | `burning` while her passive is on | size = the cone's reach (130 px) · extents = the cone, packed by `CueShapes.Cone(reach, half-angle)` — the half-extents of its bounding box; `CueShapes.ConeHalfAngle` unpacks it (40°) · magnitude = damage · direction = facing | *HandleBA* |
| `s1.cast` | — | — | magnitude = burn seconds | *HandleSkill1* |
| **loop** `s1.tornado` | — | — | size = half-width · extents = the box's half-extents (128 × 40 px) · magnitude = seconds | *ActivateTornado / EndTornado / _ExitTree* |
| `s1.tornado.tick` | tick 1–5 | — | size, extents as the loop · magnitude = tick damage | *TornadoHit* |
| `s2.cast` | — | `burning` | magnitude = waves to come · up | *HandleSkill2* |
| `s2.wave` | wave 1–3 | `burning` | magnitude = seeds in the fan (6 / 8 / 10) · up · at the fire point | *SpawnSeedWave* — one per wave, never one per seed |
| `s2.seed.expire` (class `projectile`, no source) | — | `burning` | direction = its travel · where it died on terrain | *PomeSeed.OnBodyEntered* |

Also raised under a kit's id: `pumpking` / `ba.explode` (class `projectile`; size = blast
radius, magnitude = blast damage, 0 and tag `dud` for a head that only pops) —
*PumpKingHead.Explode*.

### 6.4 World, hazards, flow

| Owner / Action | Variant | Tag | Size · Magnitude · Direction · Position · Source | Raised by |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| `world` / `soft.enter` · `soft.exit` | — | the medium: `water` · `foliage` · `kit` (a character's own volume) · or whatever its builder named it | size = the body's radius · magnitude = its speed px/s · direction = its travel · at the body · source = the body | *SoftVolume.RaiseCrossing ← the body's Enter/ExitSoftVolume* — between open air and "a medium", once per sea, not per tile; a pure current raises nothing |
| `hazard` / `tick` | — | the hazard: `fire` · `freeze` · `lava` · `spike` · `poop` · `damage` | size, extents = its box · magnitude = damage or status points · at the victim · source = the hazard · side = the victim's | *Hazard.RaiseTickCue ← Deliver* |
| `flow` / `arena.enter` | node level | the world the map was built for (`""` on the legacy arena or a map that names none); **in zone 6 the variant — `void_frontier` · `avici` (v0.12.0)**, never the world whose map it borrows (`VOID` for a VOID-touched map with no variant) | size = map width px · magnitude = backdrop lightness 0–1 (−1 = none) — **as drawn**: in zone 6 the lightness after the VOID treatment (`VoidTreatment.DrawnLightness`) · source = the arena itself: when that node leaves the tree the arena is over (there is no `arena.exit`; a listener ends its ambience then) | *GameManager._Ready* |
| `flow` / `countdown.tick` · `countdown.go` | seconds left (3, 2, 1) | — | — | *GameManager._Process* |
| `flow` / `mission.start` · `mission.success` · `mission.fail` | node level | `collection` · `protect` · `destroy` · `slaughter` · `boss` | — | *GameManager._Process · OnMissionResolved* |
| `flow` / `boss.intro` · `boss.defeated` | node level | the boss's content id | at the boss (where it stood) · source = the boss, if still there | *BossMission.StageBoss · Tick* |
| `flow` / `player.down` | — | — | at the player | *GameManager.OnPlayerDied* |
| `flow` / `run.over` | — | `death` · `boss_timer` · `victory` · `void_devoured` (v0.11.7) | — · at the eaten node for `void_devoured` | *GameManager.OnPlayerDied · OnMissionResolved · VoidDevourStep.Run* |
| `flow` / `mission.time` (v0.11.7) | whole seconds left (30, 20, 10, 5…1) | the mission type | — | *GameManager.PushMissionHud* |
| `flow` / `menu.enter` · `event.enter` (v0.11.7) | — · the day | — | — | *MenuController._Ready · EventController._Ready* |
| `flow` / `map.enter` (v0.11.7) | the day | the token's world · `VOID` | at the token (map units) | *MapController._Ready* |
| `flow` / `map.travel` (v0.11.7) | stamina spent | the destination's kind | size = distance · direction · at the destination | *MapController.TryMove* |
| `flow` / `shelter.enter` (v0.11.7) | the day | `hub` · `void` · `eidolon` | — | *ShelterController._Ready* |
| `flow` / `runover.enter` (v0.11.7) | — | `death` · `void_devoured` · `boss_timer` · `victory` | — | *RunOverController._Ready* |
| `flow` / `day.end` (v0.11.7) | the new day | `VOID` inside it | — | *RunState.EndDay* |
| `flow` / `void.devour` (v0.11.7) | the day that ended | — · `singularity` | magnitude = nodes eaten | *VoidDevourStep.Run · RunState.EnterVoid* |
| `ui` / `pause.open` · `pause.close` (v0.11.7) | — | — | — | *PauseMenu.Open · Close* |
| `ui` / `hover` · `press` · `back` (v0.11.7) | — | — | size = the button's width · at its centre (screen px) | *UiCues ← every BaseButton* (a screen calls `UiCues.Attach(this)`) |

### 6.5 Māra and his wheel — owner `z6_mara` (v0.12.3, `Docs/Mara.gdd`)

His body and his wheel share one owner, so his look and his wheel's look are one style. No
director has rows for them yet. Every cue below falls back to `boss` / `any` until the art and
music land (`Mara.gdd` §13 step 3).

| Action | Kind | Variant | Tag | Notes | Raised by |
|---|---|---|---|---|---|
| `wheel.tell` | one-shot | the realm landing (`WheelRealm`) | its id | magnitude = the tell's seconds: the sigil flares, the stone grinds | *WheelOfBecomingField.OnTell* |
| `wheel.turn` | one-shot | the realm landing | its id | the gong as it lands | *…OnLanded* |
| `wheel.pass` | one-shot | the realm passing | its id | the Last Turn, once per realm | *…OnPassed* |
| `realm` | loop | the realm | its id | while a non-human realm is in force | *…StartLoops / StopLoops* |
| `interval` | loop | — | `humans` | while the human realm is in force: the bed cuts to one bell | *…StartLoops / StopLoops* |
| `last_turn` · `liberation` | one-shot | realms to pass · — | — | magnitude = the spin's seconds | *…OnLastTurn · OnBossDied* |
| `devour.swallow` | one-shot | — | — | at the swallowed shot · magnitude = its damage | *…Swallows* |
| `offering` | one-shot | — | the poison | at the bowl | *…TickOffering* |
| `ba.tell` · `s1.tell` | one-shot | 1, or 2 under Doubt (a false tell shows) | — | magnitude = the tell's seconds | *Mara.BeginTell* |
| `ba.swing` | one-shot | the swipe (1–3) | — | cone extents | *Mara.TickSwipes* |
| `s1.cast` · `s1.catch` | one-shot | — | — | the noose thrown · a fighter caught | *Mara.ThrowNoose · NooseCaught* |
| `s2.cast` · `s2.slam` | one-shot | 1, or 2 under Doubt · — | — | the colossus's hand: its shadow · its slam (at the slam) | *Mara.HandleSkill2 · MaraStrike* |
| `realm.leap` | one-shot | 1 up, 0 down | — | onto or off the throne | *Mara.LeapTo* |
| `realm.halo_cast` · `realm.halo` · `realm.garland` | one-shot | — | — | Iron Throne's strikes | *Mara.CastHalo · MaraStrike* |
| `realm.wrath_fire` · `realm.chain_hooks` · `realm.blind_charge` | one-shot | — | — | the asuras', hell's and the animals' arrivals | *Mara* |
| `realm.gorge` | loop | — | — | the hungry ghosts' inhale | *Mara.BeginGorge / EndGorge* |
| `realm.gorge_bite` | one-shot | — | — | the bite at its end | *Mara.GorgeBite* |
| `ba.image_swing` · `image.pop` | one-shot | — | — | a mirror image's copied swipe · an image popped | *Mara.ImageSwipe · MaraImage.Pop* |

Hits name their attack the same way: `ba.swing`, `s1.bite`, `s2.slam` (ranged: the colossus's
hand never holds the emanation), `realm.halo`, `realm.gorge_bite`, `realm.chain_hook`,
`realm.blind_charge` (variant 2 from an image), `ba.image_swing`, `s1.image_catch`, and Wrath
Fire's `s1.wrath_fire`.

### 6.6 PumpKing's ultimate, the Black Prison — owner `pumpking` (v0.12.11, `Docs/PumpKing.gdd`)

The prison's own cues are raised at a position, sourced from the prison (or its pumpkin), in
the caster's class (`fighter`, or `boss` for a BOSS PumpKing's). No director has rows for them
yet: they fall back to the class and `any` until the prison's art and sound exist (PumpKing.gdd,
TODO(art)).

| Action | Kind | Variant | Size · Magnitude · Direction · Position | Raised by |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| `ult.cast` | one-shot, on him | — | size = the prison's radius (8 m since v0.12.15) · magnitude = the warning's seconds · direction = to the centre | *PumpKing.HandleSkillUlt* |
| `ult.warn` | **loop** | — | at the centre · size = the radius · magnitude = 1 s | *BlackPrison.Begin → Form (or _ExitTree)* |
| `ult.prison` | **loop** | — | at the centre · size = the radius · magnitude = 4 s | *BlackPrison.Form → End (or _ExitTree)* |
| `ult.catch` | one-shot | — | at a body as it is caught · size = its hit radius | *BlackPrison.Hold* |
| `ult.pumpkin` | one-shot | which (1–8) | where it grows · size = its radius px · magnitude = its damage · direction = its throw · source = the pumpkin | *BlackPrison.GrowPumpkin* |
| `ult.pumpkin.splat` | one-shot | — | where it burst on the ground, or ended its flight · size · direction = its travel | *PrisonPumpkin.Burst* (a pumpkin that hits a body is told by its `HitCue`) |
| `ult.recast` | one-shot, on him | — | magnitude = the mouth's seconds (0.4) · direction = to the centre | *PumpKing.HandleSkillUlt* |
| `ult.mouth` | one-shot | — | at the centre · size = half its heart (his head's 3 m blast; v0.12.13) · magnitude = 0.4 s | *BlackPrison.Recast* |
| `ult.blink` | one-shot, on him | — | where he lands · magnitude = how far px · direction | *PumpKing.LandInPrisonMouth* |
| `ult.blast` | one-shot | — | at the centre · size = its heart, his head's blast (3 m; the whole prison before v0.12.13) · magnitude = its damage | *PumpKing.LandInPrisonMouth* |

---

## 7. Comfort settings

`FeedbackSettings` (static, 0–1). Since v0.12.6 the **Settings screen** (pause menu and title,
`SettingsDialog`) has a slider for each, applied at once, and `SettingsStore` keeps them in
`settings.json` beside the save slots (following `SaveGameService`'s redirection, so a check
never touches the player's own).

| Setting | Default | Scales |
|---|---|---|
| `ScreenShake` | 1 | shake, kick, roll — and the tsunami's rumble |
| `CameraPunch` | 1 | the zoom punch (and slow-motion, when it exists) |
| `Flash` | 1 | flash strength, from full down to the 35 % tint |
| `HitStop` | 1 | every stop; 0 = off. The one setting that touches the simulation |
| `Particles` | 1 | reserved for the VFX director |
| `MasterVolume` · `MusicVolume` · `SfxVolume` · `UiVolume` | 1 · 0.8 · 1 · 0.9 | reserved for the audio director |

---

## 8. Whose style an effect wears

The universal layer in this document is the same in every world — a hit reads as a hit
everywhere [R2 B6.1, from memory]. The *effects* layer belongs to whoever caused it: a
protagonist's effects wear their home world's medium in every arena, a foe's its world's,
and dust, splashes, ambience and hazards the realm's (R2 §4.5–4.6).

| Protagonist | Style | Status |
|---|---|---|
| Pomegraknight | VK Beach — storybook watercolour | from her GDD |
| PumpKing | Dark Wood — scratchboard | from his GDD |
| Pixolotl | Forgotten City — pixel art | from the style bible |
| **Cleopastar** | **Starland (SL) — flat poster** | **provisional** — her GDD says the Palace of LOOING |
| **Sifu Pangda** | **Banboo Maze (BM) — freehand ink** | **provisional** — his GDD says Gui Lin, which has no world yet |

---

## 9. Deferred

| Deferred | Why |
|---|---|
| World-rate slow-motion (last kill, boss kill, ultimates) | The checks set `Engine.TimeScale` themselves, and a world rate has to reach foes, projectiles, hazards and effects first |
| The boss-kill freeze of every fighter | It is hit-stop, so gameplay must apply it; today `boss.defeated` is a camera beat only |
| Holding a killed foe on its flash frame | A foe frees itself the frame it dies; needs a death delay in `BaseFoe` |
| The victim's sprite shaking in place during a stop; squash and stretch | Kits animate their sprites' position and scale; needs a look at each |
| Pace scaling and per-attack multi-hit decay (R2 §4.3 rules 4, 10) | The stop budget (§4.6) bounds the worst case; the finer rules want real fights to tune against |
| The other four kits: cues, named hits, attacker stop | Next team — copy Pomegraknight (`20-ENGINEERING.md` §4). Until then their hits are `any`, hold their victims by damage, and never hold their attacker; Pixolotl and Sifu Pangda still shake the camera directly (`ShakeCamera`) |
| Particles and drawn effects; all audio; rumble; the low-HP vignette | Next teams, on this bus |
| Pooling and merging damage numbers | `DamageNumberManager` is untouched |
| The options screen; saving the settings | §7 |
| Telling a cloud from foliage; a map that serves several worlds | A cloud and a bush are tuned alike — `SoftVolume.MediumKind` is there to be named; `arena.enter` takes the first world a map lists |
| The flash shader, looked at in a renderer | Headless Godot draws nothing. At rest no body wears the material, so a wrong shader can only spoil the flash frames |

---

## 10. Verification

`Godot --headless --path . res://Scenes/Feedback/FeedbackCheck.tscn` — `40-QA.md` §(2). It
drives real bodies and proves the mechanisms above; it prints the numbers quoted here.

```
feel  a slash        15 damage is Light: the victim holds 44 ms (3 ticks), the attacker 31 ms (2) — once for the swing, however many it hit
feel  the player hit 18 of 200 HP scores 13.5 (Light): held 50 ms, direction 0.97,-0.24 away from the foe
feel  hit-stop       a 100 ms stop holds 6 ticks: moved 0.00 px running and 0.00 px in the air · out of it at 5.33 px a tick (was 5.33) and rising 9.67 (was 10.24, less one tick of gravity)
feel  shake          12 Light hits at once: trauma 0.30 (cap 0.30, 2.7 px) · 40 in a row peak 0.30 · a Heavy among them 0.43 (cap 0.75, 16.9 px)
feel  the bus        14000 cues raised with the feel director listening (shake, kick, flash): 0 bytes allocated
```

---

## 11. Decisions log

| Date | Decision | Why |
|---|---|---|
| 2026-11-25 (v0.11.2) | A cue is keyed by two strings, owner and action, resolved owner → class → `any` | No per-event string work; a new character works before it has rows |
| 2026-11-25 | Hit-stop is per body and lives in gameplay; everything else is a listener | It moves bodies in time; nothing else in feel can change a fight |
| 2026-11-25 | During a stop every clock keeps running and abilities are still read | So no DPS, cooldown or check timing moves. Smash freezes attack timing with the body (R2 §4.3 rule 8); we chose not to, and the gain-no window therefore overlaps the stop instead of following it |
| 2026-11-25 | The attacker's stop is 0.7 of the victim's, once per swing | Responsiveness; set them equal if the follow-through looks wrong |
| 2026-11-25 | The player's hits are scored by HP share and held 50–150 ms | A hit is felt by what it costs; the i-frames already last 0.8 s |
| 2026-11-25 | A stop budget: 0.18 s, refilling at 0.15 s/s | Not in the research. Unwired kits fire streams (bubbles at 20 damage each) that a re-arm alone would let hold a foe a third of the time |
| 2026-11-25 | A body that dies is not held | A foe is freed that frame; the alternative changes when babies spawn and missions resolve |
| 2026-11-25 | The flash is a shader lent to the sprites only while it runs; foes no longer blink when hit | One owner per property; blink means "cannot be hit" |
| 2026-11-25 | Dark flash at backdrop lightness ≥ 0.80 | Banboo Maze and Ghost Town (≈ 0.9) need it; a sky-blue canvas (0.76) keeps the white convention. A guess until seen |
| 2026-11-25 | Hazard and DoT pulses merge to one per 0.35 s | Under 3 Hz, whatever listens |
| 2026-11-25 | `soft.enter` / `soft.exit` are raised by the body at the edge of "a medium" | A sea is forty tiles; the body is the only thing that knows it is still in the sea |
| 2026-11-25 | Kit physics: Sifu Pangda and PumpKing's Soul Form hold; PumpKing's head and Cleopastar's star are exempt | §4.10 |
| 2026-11-25 | `FeedbackSettings.CameraPunch` added beside `ScreenShake` | R2 §4.4 lists zoom as its own switch |
| 2026-11-25 | **Provisional:** Cleopastar's style follows Starland, Sifu Pangda's follows the Banboo Maze | Needed now by the VFX and audio teams; **the owner has not confirmed either** |
| 2026-11-25 | Noted, not changed: a dashing seagull usually lands its 20-damage contact hit a tick before its 50-damage dash hit, and the i-frames eat the dash | Found by the check; contact is tested before skills each tick. A FOES balance question |
